recently my husband and i along with our  two kids traveled across the country to  mexico to see my grandpa who has  declined in health in the last few  months  he is adamant about dying in his own  home rather than moving to the u.s  so my husband built him ramps and got  him some medical equipment to help him  maneuver while he can  this trip was by no means what i call a  destination vacation as we return to our  origin  poverty  we had to bathe in buckets and could not  do it every day because there was not  enough water which by the way was not  the cleanest or even safe to drink  there was no ac in the hot summer  weather so sleeping was difficult and  the nearest store is about 40 minutes  away by car  most people get around either on foot by  donkey or try to hitch a ride on  someone's truck bed we all ended up with  diarrhea and tired without energy to go  anywhere  i had much time to reflect  there are so many lessons i took away  from this experience that i could share  with you but one lesson resonated loudly  in my mind  when i was a child i lived like this  this was my norm  but now as an adult i see things that i  did not see when i was a child  and this particular lesson i owe to my  father  he taught me that no matter what  condition i was in that i should never  expect to receive anything from anyone  much less the people that i love  right or wrong i learned never to ask  for money or gifts or even expect them  to initially always refuse it as an act  of respect to always pay back every  penny i owe  even within family members  and never  absolutely never to desire the material  possessions someone else has  as a child i knew that we were poor i  knew that i could not ask my parents for  lunch money i knew that i could not go  on school trips or have a new pair of  shoes  i knew what our economic status was  but yet i never expected to receive  anything from anyone even those who had  more than me the reason that i think  this lesson is important is because if  you feel that you are poor  no matter what your economic status is  your mindset is that of a victim  that of someone whom the world and  others around owe something because  they had better luck  either your family should help you or  the government ought to give you  something or your employer should give  you better opportunities  this mindset is a black  and it will [ __ ] you  because when you have a mindset that you  are a victim that life has handed you  bad luck and that you lack something  you don't see opportunities you don't  see possibilities  and if they are given to you  you think of the ways that it could go  wrong of the risk of the barriers and  problems to actually achieving or  obtaining that thing  i realize now that by my dad teaching me  never to expect to receive anything from  anyone  i learned respect for those of higher  financial status than i  i now have friendships with millionaires  likely because i never expected even a  dime from them but the greatest lesson  that i have taken away from it all is  that  i can achieve the things that they have  if i am willing to work for it  i now know that my own mind can stop me  from achieving greater things but i am  no different from the millionaires whom  i serve they have made sacrifices they  have seen opportunities and they have  acted upon them  in a society that tries to place our  value based on our income our home the  clothes that we wear  i can now be free  to just be me  to focus on the love that i can give the  ways that i can improve  and free myself from the victim mindset  and gratitude is where it begins  because no matter how little we have  there is always something to be thankful  for  this little act of practicing gratitude  daily can shape your mind train your  brain to see possibilities and  opportunities  and teach your heart that you are  valuable  that you are enough that you can have  the things your heart desires  that you have the ability to create  change no matter what your life  circumstances are  [Music]  and that you are complete  beautiful and worthy just as you are  no matter what marketers and social  media may try to say  you matter you are not a victim you are  a victor  so go out there and claim your victory  i thank you so much for watching if you  like this video please give it a thumbs  up and subscribe so you won't miss when  i post a new video  until next time  bye for now  you
 

